e-l164202/cala-gonone-grotta-bue-marino-cala-luna-beach-boat-trip-t462395/","https://www.expedia.com/things-to-do/cala-gonone-grotta-bue-marino-cala-luna-beach-boat-tour.a48038050.activity-details","https://theabroadguide.com/cala-gonone-bue-marino-cave-and-cala-luna-boat-tour/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Dive and snorkel the Gulf of Orosei","type":"activity","detail":"Limestone walls, caves and very clear water, with dive centres in the village.","season":[6,7,8,9],"evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.sardinia-inside.com/where-to/holiday-regions-places/cala-gonone.html","https://www.expedia.com/things-to-do/cala-gonone-grotta-bue-marino-cala-luna-beach-boat-tour.a48038050.activity-details","https://veronikasadventure.com/cala-gonone-grotta-bue-marino-cala-luna-boat-tour/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Climb and walk above the village","type":"activity","detail":"The cliffs behind town are a climbing area in their own right, and paths run out along the gulf to the coves.","season":[4,5,6,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.sardinia-inside.com/where-to/holiday-regions-places/cala-gonone.html","https://theabroadguide.com/cala-gonone-bue-marino-cave-and-cala-luna-boat-tour/","https://www.travelocity.com/things-to-do/cala-gonone-grotta-bue-marino-cala-luna-beach-boat-tour.a48038050.activity-details"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Cala Fuili","type":"swim","detail":"The last cove you can still drive to, sand and rock under a green gorge mouth, and the trailhead for the walk south.","season":[5,6,7,8,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.calagonone.eu/en/place/what-to-see/beaches","https://www.holidoit.com/en/cosa-fare/spiagge-cala-gonone","https://roadtripsandsuitcases.com/sardinia-cala-gonone/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Walk from Cala Fuili to Cala Luna","type":"trail","detail":"The coastal path over the headland, about an hour and a half each way and roughly 12 km there and back. Moderate, exposed, and it gets you to the beach without a boat.","season":[4,5,6,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":14,"urls":["https://strictlysardinia.com/cala-gonone-sardinia-guide/","https://roadtripsandsuitcases.com/sardinia-cala-gonone/","https://sardiniabella.com/en/cala-gonone-guide-things-to-know-accomodation/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Cala Mariolu","type":"swim","detail":"White and pink pebbles the locals call snow fleas, over water shallow enough to read the bottom. Effectively boat only: the land route is a hard trek off the Golgo plateau.","season":[6,7,8,9],"evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":14,"urls":["https://www.holidoit.com/en/cosa-fare/spiagge-cala-gonone","https://calagonone.com/en/what-to-see","https://www.savoringitaly.com/cala-gonone/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Gorropu canyon","type":"trail","detail":"One of the deepest gorges in Europe, inland behind Dorgali, walked up from the river bed between walls that close to a slot.","season":[4,5,6,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":14,"urls":["https://strictlysardinia.com/cala-gonone-sardinia-guide/","https://www.duepicalagonone.com/en/blog/40-how-to-spend-your-time-and-what-to-see-in-cala-gonone","https://sardiniabella.com/en/cala-gonone-guide-things-to-know-accomodation/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Selvaggio Blu - 4° Tappa","type":"trail","detail":"7 km, about 5 h, easy","ref":{"layer":"trails","cc":"IT","id":"196073"},"sources":["layer","osm"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"sources":["layer","osm"]}},{"name":"Selvaggio Blu - 3° Tappa","type":"trail","detail":"7 km, about 5 h, easy","ref":{"layer":"trails","cc":"IT","id":"196072"},"sources":["layer","osm"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"sources":["layer","osm"]}}],"nearby":{"beaches":[{"layer":"beaches","cc":"IT","id":"it-cala-luna-Q3649988","name":"Cala Luna","km":6.4,"bearing":"S","lat":40.22479,"lon":9.62654,"tier":2,"score"